<https://archive.org/details/voa-special-english-word-book>
    dcterms:title "VOA Special English Word Book: A list of words used in Special English programs on radio, television and the Internet (Voice of America, 2009), as scanned on the Internet Archive" ;
    dcterms:creator "VOA Special English, Voice of America, Washington, D.C." ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "A work of the United States Government: the title page reads \"Voice of America Washington, D.C. 20237\", and the foreword, signed \"VOA Special English Washington, D.C. 2009\", says \"The Voice of America has been broadcasting programs in Special English since 1959\" and \"The first edition was published in 1962.\" VOA's copyright statement (https://www.voanews.com/p/5338.html): \"All text, audio and video material produced exclusively by the Voice of America is in the public domain. Credit for any use of VOA material should be given to voanews.com, Voice of America, or VOA.\" It adds that voanews.com content may also contain copyrighted material licensed for VOA programming only; the word book is VOA's own. 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\"; section 105 applies in the United States. The Internet Archive item (https://archive.org/metadata/voa-special-english-word-book), uploaded by a third party, states no licence. Recorded here with the Public Domain Mark: free of known copyright. Used to check the selection only; no content was taken from it. Credited to Voice of America in this provenance, as VOA asks."@en .

<https://en.wiktionary.org/>
    dcterms:title "English Wiktionary (English entries)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Wiktionary contributors" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house — page footer: \"Definitions and other text are available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License; additional terms may apply.\", linking to https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. Used to verify the English words and the facts of usage in the notes (definitions read through https://en.wiktionary.org/api/rest_v1/page/definition/); no content was taken from it."@en .

